---
import EdgeHead from '../../components/EdgeHead.astro';
import ToolNavigation from '../../components/ToolNavigation.astro';
const stages = [
 {id:'audience',pillar:'Evaluate',title:'Start with the people you want to help.',intro:'Describe a real audience and what you know about them. Keep assumptions visible.',fields:[['audience','Who are you trying to help?','A specific group and the situation they face.'],['evidence','What do you know, and how?','Research, conversations or observations you can substantiate. Label assumptions.'],['need','What would be useful to them?','A decision, action or understanding this work should support.']]},
 {id:'positioning',pillar:'Define',title:'Choose the promise you can support.',intro:'Turn audience understanding into a clear message. An attractive claim still needs evidence.',fields:[['offer','What do you offer?','What it does, who it is for and why that matters.'],['proof','Why should someone believe it?','Specific evidence, limitations and claims that still need checking.'],['voice','How should it sound?','A few useful voice principles, with an example if you have one.']]},
 {id:'publication',pillar:'Govern',title:'Make every piece earn its place.',intro:'Choose what to publish and what needs checking. A smaller plan you can sustain is enough.',fields:[['ideas','Which ideas serve the outcome?','Choose the useful ideas and channels. You do not need a daily schedule.'],['checks','What needs to be confirmed?','Accuracy, permissions, accessibility, confidentiality and final approval.'],['plan','Who will do what, and when?','A manageable plan and a review point. Confirm arrangements with the people involved.']]},
 {id:'learning',pillar:'Elevate',title:'Listen to what happens next.',intro:'Look for evidence of usefulness. A conversation, a better question or a practical action may matter more than reactions.',fields:[['observed','What actually happened?','Record observed responses and their source. Leave blank until you have evidence.'],['meaning','What does that tell you?','Distinguish evidence from interpretation. What is still uncertain?'],['change','What will you keep or change?','Use what you learned to update the audience, message or next plan.']]}
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>Brand and Content | EDGE workspace</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/journey/journey.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/journey/brand-content.css"/><EdgeHead title="Brand and Content | EDGE workspace" description="Connect audience evidence, brand positioning, publication and learning."/></head><body>
<div class="notice">Your brief stays in this page. A content-planner handoff temporarily keeps it in this tab. No AI requests here.</div>
<div class="shell"><ToolNavigation/>
<header><div class="eyebrow"><img src="/brand/edge-mark-on-navy.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="EDGE"/>Brand &amp; Content</div><h1>Something worth saying.<br/><span>A reason to care<b class="full-stop">.</b></span></h1><div class="intro"><p>One working brief, from the people you want to help to the response you learn from. Use the tools when they help. Your judgement joins it together.</p><p class="small">Start with the audience for a full project.<br/>Jump to any stage for a focused task.</p></div></header>
<div role="group" class="bc-nav" aria-label="Workspace stages">{stages.map((s,i)=><a href={'#'+s.id}><span>0{i+1} / {s.pillar}</span><strong>{['Audience','Message','Publication','Learning'][i]}</strong></a>)}</div>
<div class="bc-layout"><main>{stages.map((s,i)=><section id={s.id} class="bc-stage" aria-labelledby={s.id+'-title'}><div class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / {s.pillar}</div><h2 id={s.id+'-title'}>{s.title}</h2><p>{s.intro}</p>{s.fields.map(([id,label,hint])=><div class="field"><label for={'bc-'+id}>{label}</label><small id={id+'-hint'}>{hint}</small><textarea id={'bc-'+id} data-label={label} data-stage={s.pillar} maxlength="6000" aria-describedby={id+'-hint'} /></div>)}{i===1&&<div class="bc-tools"><span class="eyebrow">Optional support</span><p>Use your offer, audience and evidence to explore positioning. Choose a visual palette once the message is clear.</p><button id="bc-plan-profile">Develop a brand profile →</button><a href="/tools/brand-palette">Explore a colour palette →</a></div>}{i===2&&<div class="bc-tools"><span class="eyebrow">Optional support</span><p>Bring the context you have reviewed to the content planner, then check important wording before publication.</p><button id="bc-plan-content">Plan useful content →</button><a href="/tools/before-you-send">Review a message →</a></div>}</section>)}</main>
<aside class="bc-aside"><div class="eyebrow">The thread that connects it</div><h3>Useful to someone.<br/>Grounded in something.</h3><p class="small">A brand profile, a palette and a set of posts are outputs. The purpose is to help the right people understand, decide or act.</p><div id="bc-progress" role="status">Your brief is ready to begin.</div><div class="exports"><button id="bc-copy">Copy working brief</button><button id="bc-download">Download working brief</button></div><p id="bc-status" role="status" class="small"></p><p class="small">Brand profile and content planning let you select context and return to this brief within two hours. Other tool links do not transfer your notes, so copy or download first. The existing tools have their own draft-saving behaviour.</p><img class="dare" src="/brand/dare.png" width="140" alt="DARE by democratising.ai"/></aside></div>
<footer><span>EDGE, created by Adrian Watkins</span><a href="/tools/edge-journey">A broader decision? Open your EDGE brief →</a></footer></div><dialog id="bc-handoff" aria-labelledby="bc-handoff-title"><form method="dialog"><button class="close" aria-label="Close content handoff">×</button></form><h2 id="bc-handoff-title">Choose what the planner needs.</h2><p>Only selected notes are offered to the next tool. You will review them there before they replace any current context. Nothing is sent to AI by this handoff.</p><div id="bc-handoff-items"></div><p id="bc-handoff-status" role="status"></p><button id="bc-handoff-confirm" class="primary">Continue to content planner</button></dialog><script is:inline src="/journey/brand-content.js"></script></body></html>
